 ## Background
-Originating from the `dust3r-3dgs` repository, this method is an adaptation of densification strategies for 3D Gaussian Splatting, specifically designed to work with scenes reconstructed from DUSt3R/MASt3R outputs [S1, unofficial]. It was developed to address the limitations of standard gradient-based splitting by incorporating frequency-aware metrics [S1, unofficial].
